.* MAIN: the system main menu, where a session starts.
:PNLGRP.
:COPYR.(C) COPYRIGHT QUARTZ SYSTEMS 2026.
:CLASS NAME=OPTCL BASETYPE='CHAR 3'.
:ECLASS.
:CLASS NAME=NAMECL BASETYPE='CHAR 10'.
:ECLASS.
:VAR NAME=OPTION CLASS=OPTCL.
:VAR NAME=PANELID CLASS=NAMECL VALUE='MAIN'.
:KEYL NAME=MENUKEYS.
:KEYI KEY=ENTER ACTION=ENTER.
:KEYI KEY=HELP ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F1 ACTION=HELP.
:KEYI KEY=F3 ACTION=EXIT.F3=Exit
:KEYI KEY=F4 ACTION='RETURN 4'.F4=Prompt
:KEYI KEY=F9 ACTION=RETRIEVE.F9=Retrieve
:KEYI KEY=F12 ACTION=CANCEL.F12=Cancel
:KEYI KEY=F13 ACTION='MENU INFO'.F13=Information Assistant
:KEYI KEY=F23 ACTION='RETURN 23'.F23=Set initial menu
:EKEYL.
:PANEL NAME=MAIN HELP=HLPMAIN KEYL=MENUKEYS ENTER='RETURN 1' TOPSEP=SYSNAM PANELID=PANELID.QS/400 Main Menu
:MENU DEPTH='*' SCROLL=YES OPTIONS=OPTION.Select one of the following:
:MENUI OPTION=1 ACTION='MENU USER'.User tasks
:MENUI OPTION=2 ACTION='MENU OFCTSK'.Office tasks
:MENUI OPTION=3 ACTION='MENU SYSTEM'.General system tasks
:MENUI OPTION=4 ACTION='MENU DATA'.Files, libraries, and folders
:MENUI OPTION=5 ACTION='MENU PROGRAM'.Programming
:MENUI OPTION=6 ACTION='MENU CMN'.Communications
:MENUI OPTION=7 ACTION='MENU DEFINE'.Define or change the system
:MENUI OPTION=8 ACTION='MENU PROBLEM'.Problem handling
:MENUI OPTION=9 ACTION='MENU MAJOR'.Display a menu
:MENUI OPTION=10 ACTION='MENU INFO'.Information Assistant options
:MENUI OPTION=11 ACTION='MENU ACCESS'.QS/400 Access tasks
:MENUI OPTION=90 ACTION='CMD SIGNOFF'.Sign off
:EMENU.
:CMDLINE SIZE=LONG.Selection or command
:EPANEL.
:HELP NAME=HLPMAIN.QS/400 Main Menu - Help
:P.The main menu is where a session begins. Type an option number or a
command on the line at the bottom and press Enter. Option 9 shows the
command menus; option 90 signs off.
:P.F3 leaves the menu (signing off when it is the session's first),
F4 prompts the command typed, F9 brings the previous command back,
F12 returns to the menu shown before this one, F23 makes this menu
the one the user's sessions start with.
:EHELP.
:EPNLGRP.
